# Validation 1: a Builder wish. The Wish Builder (on the watch, or /moddy builder) walks the player through chest pages
# (what kind, which body, parts, powers, special moves) to a "Tune" dialog, and "Make it!" makes the thing. No AI.
# The pages are chests of different sizes, so each page's "Done" tile is at a different slot: the middle of its last
# row (6 rows: 49, 4 rows: 31, 3 rows: 22). If the Builder's pages change, re-read the slots from the frames.
@intent The Wish Builder's pages, clicked like a player, make a creature that appears in the world

@step a clear stage
gamemode creative
time set noon
weather clear
gamerule advance_time false
gamerule spawn_mobs false
tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 10

@step open the Wish Builder
/moddy builder
@expect screen Wish Builder within 10s
@shot what-shall-we-make

@step a creature, from the first body (a cat)
@click slot 0
@expect screen Pick a body within 5s
@click slot 0
@expect screen Parts within 5s
@shot parts

@step no extra parts, powers or moves
@click slot 49
@expect screen Powers within 5s
@click slot 31
@expect screen Special moves within 5s
@click slot 22
@expect screen /tune your/ within 5s
@shot tune-dialog

@step make it
@click button "Make it!"
@expect chat is ready within 120s
@wait 2s
@shot the-wish-made

@step the creature is in the world
# A wished creature's body carries the tags wishmob and mfamrig ("Buddy the Cat" here).
@repeat 10 until execute if entity @e[tag=wishmob,tag=mfamrig]
@wait 1s
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @e[tag=wishmob,tag=mfamrig,distance=..60]
